  "captions": {
    "data-branch-disposition": "Branch disposition for all eight mechanisms under strict (S) and on-reach (R) games. Each row retains all 40,960 planned slots from 128 trials. Stacked statuses partition completed, invalid, failed and unstarted branches; narrow budget-control segments remain in the exact source counts. Inactive-held branches are a subset of completed branches, displayed separately with exact counts. Completed execution includes known violations and unknown target evidence and does not imply outcome verification or an available coefficient vector.",
    "data-interval-tradeoffs": "On-reach global-consequence retry coefficient for every registered mechanism. Normal and Hoeffding intervals use identical retained draws. A/R gives two counts: available estimates and population-reference-eligible trials, respectively, each from 128 planned trials per case. A/R is not a coverage fraction. Coverage is conditional on availability and a defined reference; whiskers are nominal 95% Wilson uncertainty for repeated-trial rates. Mean widths show the precision cost. Filled sign-panel symbols report correct reference-sign detection for nonzero coefficients; open symbols report false nonzero flags at zero references. Undefined lagged evidence and budget refusals are not zero coverage. Rows and interval methods share data and are not independent replications."
  },
